  "description": "The document value space (Phase 644, DECISIONS.md D260), through the cases of capability-laws.json: `validateArgs`, `invocationKey`, `declarationRoundTrip` and `pipelineTypeCheck`, each read exactly as that file describes it. Authored inputs, each `expected` computed by calling the pinned kit; no seed. Every vector is stated over one capability, `cap-document`: a single required hole `d0` in the document space of type `Order`, answering a document of type `Receipt`. `capability` and `declaration` members carry a canonical capability declaration as a JSON STRING, in which a document space is `{\"$type\":\"document\"}` with an optional `documentType`. A document argument is a member exactly when it is well-formed JSON with a canonical rendering of its own: it parses with no `null`, and holds no repeated member, no ill-formed string and no number a finite float cannot spell. The type name is carried and never read. An argument that is no document is `argOutOfSpace` at its address. The two `document-key-*` vectors present ONE document in two spellings (members out of order, white space, a float with a trailing zero, a control character by its short escape) and expect one key: an argument in a document space is keyed by its cross-host canonical text (members sorted, no white space, the canonical float layout, every control character as `\\u00xx`). They carry no `capturedValue`. The `document-pipeline-output-*` vectors pin the space relation: a document result is admitted by a declared output of the same type or of no type, and by no other document type, no scalar space and no tree space.",
